# foo (Pyro plugin)

Fetch the SDK once:

    go mod tidy

Then build, install and rebuild on every save (a running `pyro serve` picks changes up):

    pyro plugin dev .

Try one call of the installed plugin:

    pyro plugin test foo --url foo://localhost:1234 --body hello

Or build and install by hand:

    GOOS=wasip1 GOARCH=wasm go build -buildmode=c-shared -o foo.wasm .
    pyro plugin install .

Package for sharing (prints the sha256 for an index entry):

    pyro plugin pack .

See docs/plugins.md in the Pyro repository for the SDK and ABI.
